{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:type handlerEntry","summary":"handlerEntry now holds a two-step breaker plus a per-handler watches context and cancel func. Reconcile uses these to end watches when a backend is replaced or removed.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"handlerEntry gains two-step breaker and per-handler watch context","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Struct fields added and breaker type changed, which alters lifecycle and concurrency behavior of served watches.","risk_signals":["struct fields added","concurrency","context cancellation lifecycle"],"focus":["every handlerEntry construction site sets watches/endWatches (tests build entries literally with nil watches)","endWatches is called exactly once per retired entry"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:newHandlerEntry","summary":"New constructor creates a cancelable watches context and a fresh breaker for each entry. Reconcile uses it for both new and changed groups.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"New constructor gives each handler its own cancelable watch context","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Creates a cancelable context per handler; a missed cancel leaks the context and leaves watches running.","risk_signals":["context lifecycle","resource leak if not cancelled"],"focus":["every entry created here is eventually passed to endWatches, including when reconcile returns early or errors"]},
