{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:NewGrafanaRouter","summary":"The router now creates a router-wide cancelable watches context at construction, used to end all watches at shutdown.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Router creates a router-wide cancelable watch context","confidence":0.75,"reason":"Introduces a cancelable context whose lifetime governs all watches; shutdown behavior depends on it.","risk_signals":["context lifecycle","shutdown behavior"],"focus":["closeWatches is always called on every stop path"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:(*GrafanaRouter).reconcile","summary":"Changed groups now get a new handlerEntry instead of being mutated in place, and replaced or removed entries have their watches ended after the new snapshot is published, so clients re-watch against the new backend.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Reconcile replaces entries and ends watches of retired backends","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Changes replacement semantics and terminates in-flight watch streams when the backend key changes or a group is removed.","risk_signals":["concurrency","streams terminated on reconcile","entry replaced rather than mutated"],"focus":["endWatches runs after publish, so a re-watching client always lands on the new entry","anything holding the old *handlerEntry pointer across reconcile","breaker state for an unchanged key is still preserved"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:(*GrafanaRouter).publish","summary":"The published servingEntry now copies the handler's watches context so request serving can bind watches to it.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Publish copies the watches context into serving entries","confidence":0.7,"reason":"One extra field copied into the snapshot that the serving path uses to end watches; low risk but tied to watch lifecycle.","risk_signals":["concurrency","watch lifecycle"],"focus":["entries built without watches (nil) are handled by serveWatch"]}
]}

