{"id":"pkg/router/breaker.go:type statusRecorder","summary":"statusRecorder gains an onStatus callback field used to report the breaker outcome as soon as the status is written. It is set only by serveThroughBreaker.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"statusRecorder gets an onStatus callback hook","confidence":0.7,"reason":"New field carries the breaker-reporting hook that changes when outcomes are recorded; reviewed together with WriteHeader and serveThroughBreaker.","risk_signals":["breaker accounting timing"],"focus":["that onStatus is only set where the once-guard in serveThroughBreaker applies"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker.go:(*statusRecorder).WriteHeader","summary":"WriteHeader now invokes onStatus with the final status (non-1xx, or 101) before forwarding to the underlying writer. This is what lets the breaker learn the outcome when a watch starts rather than when it ends.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"WriteHeader reports final status to breaker callback","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Runs a callback in the response path, changing when breaker outcomes are recorded.","risk_signals":["callback in response path","breaker accounting timing"],"focus":["the callback runs before the underlying WriteHeader and must not block","proxy failure is recorded before the 502 status is written by the error handler"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker.go:type groupBreaker","summary":"Introduces a type alias for gobreaker's two-step circuit breaker, replacing the one-step type across the router.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"refactor","headline":"Add groupBreaker alias for the two-step breaker","confidence":0.8,"reason":"A type alias only; behavior change lives in newGroupBreaker and serveThroughBreaker.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker.go:newGroupBreaker","summary":"Group breakers are now created as two-step breakers with the same settings, so callers must use Allow and report an outcome. Every consumer of the breaker (router, ST fallback) is affected.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Group breakers now constructed as two-step breakers","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Changes the breaker's calling contract and thus how all proxied requests are counted.","risk_signals":["breaker semantics"],"focus":["every user of the breaker (including the ST fallback) goes through serveThroughBreaker and reports exactly one outcome"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker.go:serveThroughBreaker","summary":"Replaces cb.Execute with Allow plus a once-guarded done callback, reported on status write, on return, or on panic. A half-open breaker's trial slot is freed when a watch's status is known instead of when it ends, and a re-panic is preserved.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Breaker outcome reported at status write, not handler return","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Concurrency, panic handling and breaker accounting changed on the main proxy path.","risk_signals":["concurrency","panic recovery","breaker accounting timing","error handling changed"],"focus":["exactly one outcome is reported on every path, including panic and no-WriteHeader returns","failures after a 200 status (mid-stream errors) are no longer counted against the backend","outcome computed in onStatus sees the proxy failure recorded before the status is written","panic with a nil outcome is reported as a failure and re-panicked unchanged"]},
