{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:(*GrafanaRouter).HandleFunc","summary":"Upgrade requests to routed groups now get a 400, and watch requests run through serveWatch scoped to the owning backend entry. A watch ends when the backend is replaced or removed, and clients re-watch.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Routed watches get lifecycle scope; upgrade requests rejected with 400","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Changes request handling on the proxy path: a new rejection response and a context-cancellation lifecycle for watches.","risk_signals":["new 400 response for upgrade requests","context cancellation","concurrency"],"focus":["clients that rely on Connection: Upgrade to routed groups, which now get a 400","a watch that arrives just as its entry is retired ends immediately and the client retries against the new snapshot","requestVerb classification of non-resource paths such as discovery"]},
