{"id":"pkg/router/watch.go","summary":"New helpers classify requests with the apiserver RequestInfoFactory, reject upgrades, and run watches under a cancellable context tied to the backend scope and router shutdown. A router-initiated end is turned from an aborted response into a clean stream end by swallowing http.ErrAbortHandler.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"New watch lifecycle: scoped cancellation, clean end, upgrade rejection","confidence":0.9,"reason":"New concurrency and panic-recovery logic on the live proxy path that decides how watch streams end.","risk_signals":["concurrency","panic recovery","context cancellation","public API behavior"],"focus":["the recover swallows ErrAbortHandler only when the router's own context ended and the request context did not","context.AfterFunc cleanup, so no goroutine or registration leaks per watch","requestVerb fallback to the lowercased method when RequestInfo fails or the verb is empty","HeaderValuesContainsToken handles multi-valued or comma-separated Connection headers"]}
